{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Sri Lankan sambar deer ("Rusa unicolor unicolor") is a subspecies of sambar deer that lives in Sri Lanka.","title":"Sri Lankan sambar deer"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This subspecies is one of the largest sambar deer species with the largest antlers both in size and in body proportions.","title":"Sri Lankan sambar deer"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Large males weight up to 270–280 kg.","title":"Sri Lankan sambar deer"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Sri Lankan sambar live in lowland dry forests and mountain forests.","title":"Sri Lankan sambar deer"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Large herds of sambar deer roam the Horton Plains National Park, where it is the most common large mammal.","title":"Sri Lankan sambar deer"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Visayan spotted deer ("Rusa alfredi"), also known as the Philippine spotted deer, is a nocturnal and endangered species of deer located primarily in the rainforests of the Visayan islands of Panay and Negros though it once roamed other islands such as Cebu, Guimaras, Leyte, Masbate, and Samar.","title":"Visayan spotted deer"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is one of three endemic deer species in the Philippines, although it was not recognized as a separate species until 1983.","title":"Visayan spotted deer"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" An estimated 2,500 mature individuals survived worldwide as of 1996, according to the IUCN, although it is uncertain of how many of them still survive in the wild.","title":"Visayan spotted deer"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The diet of the deer, which consists of a variety of different types of grasses, leaves, and buds within the forest, is the primary indicator of its habitat.","title":"Visayan spotted deer"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Since 1991 the range of the species has severely decreased and is now almost co-extensive with that of the Visayan warty pig.","title":"Visayan spotted deer"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Europe, the Caucasus, Asia Minor, Iran, western and central Asia, the Atlas Mountains of north‑western Africa, and introduced populations in Australia, New Zealand, the United States, Canada, Peru, Uruguay, Chile and Argentina.
Evidence: {"sentence_id":1,"text":" The red deer inhabits most of Europe, the Caucasus Mountains region, Asia Minor, Iran, parts of western Asia, and central Asia.","title":"Red deer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" It also inhabits the Atlas Mountains region between Morocco and Tunisia in northwestern Africa, being the only species of deer to inhabit Africa.","title":"Red deer"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Red deer have been introduced to other areas, including Australia, New Zealand, United States, Canada, Peru, Uruguay, Chile and Argentina.","title":"Red deer"}"],"previous_answer":"noanswer","question":"What are some other areas that share a common deer species with the forests of Mara and Mondrem?"}

{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sophie Lara Winkleman (born 5 August 1980) is an English actress.","title":"Sophie Winkleman"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" As the wife of Lord Frederick Windsor, son of Queen Elizabeth II's first cousin Prince Michael of Kent, she is formally referred to as Lady Frederick Windsor, but continues to use her maiden name in her professional career.","title":"Sophie Winkleman"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"ElvenQuest is a comic fantasy broadcast on BBC Radio 4 by Anil Gupta and Richard Pinto, and starring Stephen Mangan, Alistair McGowan, Darren Boyd, Kevin Eldon, Sophie Winkleman and Dave Lamb.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series takes place in the world of Lower Earth, a parody of Middle-earth from "The Lord of the Rings" by J. R. R. Tolkien.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In Lower Earth, a band of warriors go forth to search for a mythical sword to save Lower Earth from the evil Lord Darkness (played by McGowan).","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In order to do so, they must find "The Chosen One" who will save Lower Earth.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Chosen One is Amis, a dog in the real world which belongs to a fantasy novelist called Sam Porter (played by Mangan).","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The first series was broadcast from 29 March to 3 June 2009 and the second from 18 November 2010.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The third series began broadcasting from 17 October 2011.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The fourth series began broadcasting 12 February 2013.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Comic fantasy is a subgenre of fantasy that is primarily humorous in intent and tone.","title":"Comic fantasy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Usually set in imaginary worlds, comic fantasy often includes puns on and parodies of other works of fantasy.","title":"Comic fantasy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text"