{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Erie Canal: Second Genesee Aqueduct, also known as the Broad Street Aqueduct or Broad Street Bridge, is a historic stone aqueduct located at Rochester in Monroe County, New York.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was constructed in 1836-1842 and originally carried the Erie Canal over the Genesee River.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The overall length of the aqueduct including the wings and abutments is 800 ft .","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The aqueduct is 70 ft wide and has massive parapets on either side.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It is one of four major aqueducts in the mid-19th century Erie Canal system.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 1927, a roadbed was added to carry automobile traffic and named Broad Street.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It also carried a part of the Rochester Subway.","title":"Broad Street Bridge (Rochester, New York)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"There are three outfall canals in New Orleans, Louisiana – the 17th Street, Orleans Avenue and London Avenue canals.","title":"New Orleans Outfall Canals"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" These canals are a critical element of New Orleans’ flood control system, serving as drainage conduits for much of the city.","title":"New Orleans Outfall Canals"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" There are 13 mi of levees and floodwalls that line the sides of the canals.","title":"New Orleans Outfall Canals"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 17th Street Canal is the largest and most important drainage canal and is capable of conveying more water than the Orleans Avenue and London Avenue Canals combined.","title":"New Orleans Outfall Canals"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: The 17th Street Canal is in New Orleans, Louisiana (along the boundary with Metairie), and the Beaver and Erie Canal is in western Pennsylvania.
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 17th Street Canal is the largest and most important drainage canal in the city of New Orleans.","title":"17th Street Canal"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 17th Street Canal forms a significant portion of the boundary between the city of New Orleans and Metairie, Louisiana.","title":"17th Street Canal"}
